  "description": "The per-neutron (q^2+1)^2 cancellation in the convention-D atomic Markov trace fires iff SOME GENERATOR carries two or more averaged crossings. Twelve 3-strand configurations; the rule holds on all twelve. Composition does not determine the outcome: a proton word with the neutron's exact template composition still cancels 0, and a neutron word with the proton's still cancels 2. Not gen0-specific (two averaged on gen1 behaves identically) and it saturates (three on one generator still cancels 2). The physical content is isospin placement: the neutron (udd) puts both averaged ud-couplings on one generator, the proton (uud) spreads its two across both -- both nucleons have exactly two. The Hecke-collapse reading in the docstring is an INTERPRETATION; the falsifiable content is the max(g0avg,g1avg) >= 2 criterion and its saturation. Scope-(a): these twelve configurations under bring_color_weighted at convention D.",
